// anti-slop/no-runtime-typeof
// A runtime `typeof` check narrows a representation without establishing a contract:
// it proves the shape of a value at one point but carries no evidence forward.
// Decode external input into a domain type at the I/O boundary, then branch on that.
// Ported from oxlint-plugin-anti-slop `no-runtime-typeof`.
// A TS type query (`type T = typeof x`, `keyof typeof x`, `x as typeof y`) is a
// different node and is not matched, exactly as in the original.
// Gap: the original's opt-in `allowInTypeGuards: true` exempts a `typeof` whose
// nearest enclosing function returns a type predicate. GritQL plugins take no
// options and cannot walk the parent chain, so this port always behaves as the
// rule's default (`allowInTypeGuards: false`) and flags type guards too.
`typeof $operand` as $node where {
	register_diagnostic(
		span = $node,
		message = "anti-slop/no-runtime-typeof: A `typeof` check narrows a representation without establishing its contract. Parse input at its I/O boundary, then branch on the domain value.",
		severity = "error"
	)
}
